Landing review corrections for Round r3 are complete across all allowlisted files.

The wave animation delays now start with a 0.8s base offset so the entry pulse completes cleanly, `.day.today` no longer runs the entry pulse, count wave cresting relies on brightness and text-shadow without scale transforms to prevent cell scroll overflow, expression glow highlights use shipped color `#b4677b`, `calendarCacheCells` queries counts directly from `numberValue`, and the Playwright day-click test verifies the selected day through the runtime state.

### What works now
1. [calendar.css](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-calendar/public/color-polish/scenes/calendar.css): Delayed `calendarWave` and `calendarWaveCount` by `calc(0.8s + var(--day-index, 0) * 0.35s)`, preserved the 60ms stagger on `.day.past` entry pulse, removed entry pulse from `.day.today`, eliminated transform scale on `b` in `calendarWaveCount` in favor of `filter: brightness(1.12)` and `text-shadow`, and aligned the highlight color stop in `calendarRowGlowB` with `#b4677b`.
2. [calendar.js](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-calendar/public/color-polish/scenes/calendar.js): `calendarCacheCells` now constructs the month day key from `el.dataset.day` and reads `numberValue('d:' + key + ':rec')` instead of relying on zeroed text nodes during mount.
